  s0 -.-x|"cannot use: the MCP client, yargs, and the Gherkin parser each have one home. Library code does not grow a second one."| k0
  s1 -.-x|"cannot use: the CLI may parse argv with yargs. The MCP client stays behind a dynamic import of the mcp module, and feature files are parsed by the feature module."| k1
  s2 -.-x|"cannot use: mcp is the only module that links the optional MCP client. It does not parse argv or feature files."| k2
